50% multiple choice, <- 20 questions, 50% code reading and writing
topics
    Normalization more in focus
        - first normal from
            - one value per cell
        - second normal from
            - each table has a key that indicates the rest of the columns
            - has to be in first normal from
        - third normal from
            - the key is the primary way to identify the data in the other columns
            - it is alloud for there to be other keys
            - no transitive relationships (a subtable in this table)
            - has to be in second normal form
        - does not make the tables simpler or easier to understand
        - updates more reliable
        - adding values faster
        Vocabulary of Database Analysis
    Database design using the metadata functions
        - once we have a design we should be able to write
            - Create table queries
            - Alter table queries
            - drop table (don't do this without backing up the database/table)
        - use of the "serial" for auto increment
        - use of the "primary key" in create table to create an index
        - the habit of using <table>_<attribute> for foriegn keys
            - keys into other tables from this table
                - registrations
                    -> students_id as a foreign key into the students table column id
                    -> courses_crn as a foreign key into the courses table column crn
            - reason 
                - students join registrations on students.id=registrations.student_id
                - students join registrations on students.id=student_id
